compile of BindParam will produce one placeholder with one parameter.\r\n<!-- A clear and concise description of what you expected to happen. -->\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\n```py\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.sql.expression import bindparam\r\n\r\nclause = bindparam('key', value=[('1', '2'), ('3', '4')], expanding=True)\r\n\r\ncompiled_query  = clause.compile(compile_kwargs={'render_postcompile': True})\r\n\r\nprint(compiled_query)  # '((:key_1_1, :key_1_2), (:key_2_1, :key_2_2))'\r\nprint(compiled_query.params)  # {'key_1_1': ('1', '2'), 'key_1_2': ('3', '4')}\r\n```\r\n**Versions.**\r\n - OS: os X 11.2 (20D64)\r\n - Python: Python 3.9.1\r\n - SQLAlchemy: 1.4.1\r\n - Database: postgres\r\n - DBAPI: any\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\nSame code for SQLAlchemy: 1.3.20 produced different results\r\n```py\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.sql.expression import bindparam\r\n\r\nclause = bindparam('key', value=[('1', '2'), ('3', '4')], expanding=True)\r\n\r\ncompiled_query  = clause.compile()\r\n\r\nprint(compiled_query)  # '([EXPANDING_key])'\r\nprint(compiled_query.params)  # {'key': [('1', '2'), ('3', '4')]}\r\n```\r\n<!-- Add any other context about the problem here. -->\r\n\r\n**Have a nice day!**\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","even